http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/53/En-us-cut.ogg
and this
http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/ce/En-us-nut.ogg
respectively, then you're not pronouncing them like {kyt} and {nyt}
([k=C9=99t] and [n=C9=99t]), but more like {kat} and {nat} ([k=C9=90t] and =
[n=C9=90t]
(international IPA)). If you're not pronouncing them similarly to how
they're pronounced in those recordings then I would be most grateful
if one of you could record him-/herself pronouncing either "cut" or
"nut" or both and upload the recording somewhere so that I can hear
your pronunciation.

